id: weather-resistant
name: Weather Resistant
kind: crafting
# "Quality Slots: 1~3" - which, asked when it is added.
slots: 1~3
# "When you gain this Quality, choose any type of Battle Weather."
chooses: weather
prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in the Survival Skill
source: Core Rule
description: >
  One Battle Weather, chosen when it is made, felt a Weather Tier lower for each Slot it takes -
  and not at all at 0. Needs 2+ Ranks in Survival in whoever wears it.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: When you gain this Quality, choose any type of Battle Weather. Treat the Weather
  Tier as if it was x Weather Tiers lower, where x is equal to the number of Quality Slots
  occupied by this Apparel Quality. If this would treat the Weather Tier as if it was 0 or less,
  completely ignore the effects of that Battle Weather.
text: >
  Weather Resistant: Built to withstand extreme weather, this clothing protects you from one
  specific weather type.
  –Apparel Category: All
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in the Survival Skill
  –Quality Slots: 1~3
  –Effects: When you gain this Quality, choose any type of Battle Weather. Treat the Weather Tier
  as if it was x Weather Tiers lower, where x is equal to the number of Quality Slots occupied by
  this Apparel Quality. If this would treat the Weather Tier as if it was 0 or less, completely
  ignore the effects of that Battle Weather.

---

# The Weather and its Slots are asked when it is added. While worn by someone with 2+ Ranks in
# Survival, standing in that Weather: every (WT) and every "Tier 2+" of it reads the Tier lower,
# and at 0 none of it is gathered. The Tier on the Battlefields tab stays the one set - it is the
# Weather's, not theirs.

[passive]
if (survival.ranks >= 2) {
  piece.resistsWeather.$choice += $slots;
}
